        ":question/id": "06b0b1bd-ae5d-56cf-89fa-4d6392983b6e",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int (5{e}^{x}+{4}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{e}^{x}+{4}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{e}^{x}+\\frac{{4}^{x}}{ln\u20614}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
