        ":question/problem": "$\\int (2{e}^{x}-{7}^{x}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{e}^{x}-{7}^{x}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {7}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-\\frac{{7}^{x}}{ln\u20617}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
